                        <p>Daniel Adams was arrested on 12 May 1794 but saved himself from prosecution by turning
    King's evidence in <persName key="TOO01">Horne Tooke's</persName> trial.  It seems unlikely that Godwin's relationship would have continued after he provided 
    evidence against Tooke and there is a more likely candidate for later 'Adams' entries - <persName key="ADA04">Joseph Adams</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Albert Goodwin, <title>The friends of liberty: the English democratic movement in the age 
